WEBVTT

00:48.173 --> 00:50.717
You think I should live with you?

00:51.301 --> 00:52.260
Mm-hmm.

00:52.343 --> 00:54.012
It'd make me so happy.

00:55.889 --> 00:57.640
You could live here. Say you will.

01:04.397 --> 01:08.234
You sure it's a good idea?
It's not too fast for you?

01:11.404 --> 01:13.073
I can handle notifying everyone

01:13.156 --> 01:14.908
and returning all the gifts
we've received.

01:14.991 --> 01:17.285
But I'm keeping the honeymoon refund.
That's fair.

01:20.538 --> 01:24.334
We were together for ten years,
and I barely know you.

01:28.338 --> 01:29.839
What was it all for?

01:30.507 --> 01:32.926
It's such a long time
to spend with someone.

01:33.968 --> 01:37.764
Yet I never fully knew
if we really loved each other.

01:47.107 --> 01:49.442
It wasn't the right match and we knew it.

01:51.569 --> 01:54.823
I'm glad we figured it out
instead of waiting even longer.

01:55.782 --> 01:58.243
That's true.

01:58.785 --> 02:02.163
It's kinda scary that it took us
ten years, though, right?

02:09.462 --> 02:12.215
I don't want to waste
another decade of my life.

02:14.425 --> 02:16.010
I want to get to know you,

02:16.636 --> 02:19.889
and find out if we're compatible
by living together.

02:20.849 --> 02:24.310
That way, it won't be long
until we know if we're gonna work.

02:24.894 --> 02:26.437
I should move in to get to know you?

02:26.521 --> 02:27.522
Mm-hmm.

02:28.356 --> 02:31.901
And since we agreed to lay low at work
since we have to be careful,

02:31.985 --> 02:35.822
doesn't it make sense for us
to optimize our time outside of work?

02:37.073 --> 02:39.742
Hmm, if it's honestly
just about efficiency,

02:40.326 --> 02:41.995
then I'm not down.

02:44.914 --> 02:46.082
You're not?

02:46.166 --> 02:47.625
I'm not.

02:49.127 --> 02:49.961
Why?

02:50.044 --> 02:54.549
First of all, I'm not taking such
a big step to "optimize" a relationship.

02:54.632 --> 02:57.760
There's a lot more to living together
than getting to know each other quickly.

02:58.386 --> 03:00.847
If it wasn't good, I'd wanna
talk about it, not call it off.

03:01.681 --> 03:05.643
So if it's just a big test,
then I won't move in with you for now.

03:07.187 --> 03:08.605
You don't even wanna try?

03:08.688 --> 03:11.065
'Cause I've done it before, moving in.

03:18.239 --> 03:21.284
You have to tell me why.
We're not breaking up out of nowhere.

03:21.868 --> 03:23.870
- I got tired.
- Of what?

03:23.953 --> 03:25.205
Living like this.

03:25.288 --> 03:27.290
You're the reason why we live like this.

03:27.373 --> 03:30.084
- You said you wanted to.
- I did. You're not wrong.

03:30.585 --> 03:31.961
And it wasn't what I thought it'd be.

03:32.045 --> 03:34.547
It feels like we'll never fully grow up.

03:35.048 --> 03:36.758
And I want more from life than this.

03:38.468 --> 03:39.510
I'm sorry.

04:00.657 --> 04:02.533
What do you mean hold off?

04:03.618 --> 04:05.161
Why would you want to put it off?

04:05.245 --> 04:06.162
Wait.

04:06.996 --> 04:08.122
Because of me?

04:08.206 --> 04:11.084
I don't totally know.

04:11.751 --> 04:12.794
What?

04:13.378 --> 04:14.796
I just thought…

04:14.879 --> 04:17.048
when I got married,
I'd be happier with you.

04:18.424 --> 04:20.260
But right now, that doesn't seem true.

04:20.343 --> 04:23.012
We fight all the time
and you're always mad.

04:23.096 --> 04:26.015
Most days, you're a totally
different person from who I married.

04:26.641 --> 04:28.685
What changed, exactly? How am I different?

04:29.269 --> 04:30.311
You were ambitious.

04:31.479 --> 04:33.314
You were smart, but not full of yourself.

04:33.398 --> 04:35.149
And you were thoughtful and kind.

04:35.233 --> 04:37.986
But mostly, you were ambitious and…

04:38.736 --> 04:39.654
And now?

04:40.697 --> 04:41.656
I'm not any longer?

04:42.907 --> 04:44.784
You never wanna plan ahead.

04:50.957 --> 04:54.127
Is this about needing a loan
to get our next place?

04:56.754 --> 04:57.672
It is.

05:01.509 --> 05:05.346
If we register, make everything official,
and get the newlywed loan,

05:05.430 --> 05:06.723
what's the plan after that?

05:07.348 --> 05:10.977
Before we can finish off
paying the loan, rent is gonna go up.

05:11.060 --> 05:13.521
Then we'll need another loan
'cause we have to move again.

05:13.604 --> 05:14.981
Do we take out loans forever?

05:15.565 --> 05:17.817
We're both young.
We have plenty of time for that.

05:17.900 --> 05:20.028
What's the plan
when we're not young anymore?

05:20.611 --> 05:22.488
Ten years to pay back the first loan.

05:22.572 --> 05:24.615
And if we win the lottery
to own an apartment,

05:24.699 --> 05:28.077
that's 20 years paying a mortgage,
which is basically renting.

05:28.161 --> 05:30.371
And after that, we'll need
to think about retiring

05:30.455 --> 05:33.624
because I'm sure I don't still
wanna be working here when I'm old.

05:33.708 --> 05:35.752
That's just how it works, Yu-jin.

05:35.835 --> 05:37.587
Well, no one told me about that.

05:41.382 --> 05:43.426
It took a lot to get to our wedding day.

05:43.509 --> 05:45.636
We worked so hard, it should be easier.

05:46.137 --> 05:49.724
Why does it feel like we're poor?
We work, but everything feels unstable.

05:52.310 --> 05:55.980
So did you think getting married
would make things easy?

05:58.816 --> 05:59.942
No, I don't know.

06:01.319 --> 06:05.239
But I don't wanna register
until I figure out what we're doing.

06:18.586 --> 06:20.380
It seems so important.

06:21.005 --> 06:23.925
I probably wanted to avoid
making the same mistakes.

06:25.218 --> 06:29.764
I've never let someone get so close
as quickly as I wanted him to.

06:29.847 --> 06:32.975
I know you're trying
not to get hurt again.

06:34.394 --> 06:35.395
Yeah, that's right.

06:36.354 --> 06:37.605
I am, too.

06:38.815 --> 06:40.316
But he says that

06:40.400 --> 06:44.445
if we get together too quickly,
we're more likely to be disappointed

06:44.529 --> 06:46.614
by little things that don't matter.

06:47.448 --> 06:49.492
And it would hurt even more
if we called it off.

06:50.827 --> 06:54.956
I know we want to open up,
but we need to protect ourselves too.

06:57.583 --> 07:01.587
How do we compromise closeness?
What's the optimal distance?

07:01.671 --> 07:06.801
EPISODE 7
OZONE WARNING

07:11.305 --> 07:12.265
Oh…

07:13.850 --> 07:15.143
It's smaller than I thought.

07:15.226 --> 07:19.397
Well, rent for this tiny thing
is at the very top of your budget.

07:19.480 --> 07:22.567
There's a waitlist for this place,
just to tour.

07:22.650 --> 07:24.152
I think we should keep looking.

07:24.235 --> 07:27.447
If this is too small, we should
really raise your budget.

07:27.530 --> 07:30.116
You'd be amazed at how much better
it gets if you go a little higher.

07:32.702 --> 07:35.121
Just let me know if there's
anything else at this price.

07:35.746 --> 07:37.123
O… kay.

07:37.206 --> 07:38.791
Thank you very much.

08:25.713 --> 08:27.673
Stay out of trouble.
I'll be back real quick.

08:29.217 --> 08:30.426
You got one for me too?

08:31.636 --> 08:32.595
See you later.

09:06.003 --> 09:07.421
Forty thousand.

09:08.172 --> 09:09.382
Hey!

09:11.676 --> 09:13.678
- All right, all right.
- All in.

09:15.429 --> 09:18.015
- Yeah, come on!
- I got it!

09:20.393 --> 09:22.603
- Now, now.
- I'll call. I'll call.

09:22.687 --> 09:24.397
Let's see who's gonna take it.

09:24.480 --> 09:25.982
- Oh, come on!
- Come on!

09:26.065 --> 09:28.859
- Let's see what you got.
- Come on!

09:28.943 --> 09:30.861
- Two fives.
- Let's go. You're done!

09:30.945 --> 09:32.280
- I got two nines.
- Hey!

09:35.366 --> 09:37.952
Shut up and shuffle the cards.

09:38.035 --> 09:39.912
Okay, again. Just one drink.

09:39.996 --> 09:42.748
Hey, shuffle already.
We ain't got all day.

09:42.832 --> 09:44.709
Come on. Hurry up.

10:02.476 --> 10:05.730
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

10:57.156 --> 10:58.866
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

11:38.030 --> 11:40.408
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

12:30.624 --> 12:33.419
Excuse me. Do you have
any shampoo that I can use?

12:35.004 --> 12:36.213
Ah, thank you so much.

12:37.214 --> 12:39.467
Huh?

12:41.886 --> 12:44.638
MALE SHOWER ROOM

13:03.449 --> 13:05.242
NIGHT-DUTY ROOM

13:10.289 --> 13:12.708
Man, he acts like he lives here
or something.

13:14.877 --> 13:16.045
- Hello.
- Hey.

13:16.128 --> 13:19.715
Some extremely hot sunlight
is telling us summer is finally here.

13:19.799 --> 13:23.969
UV levels will be very high
in those areas today.

13:24.053 --> 13:26.597
And ozone concentration
will be high as well.

13:26.680 --> 13:28.390
Don't forget to put on sunblock

13:28.474 --> 13:30.559
- before you go out…
- Wow! This place is great.

13:34.230 --> 13:35.898
Is anyone using the top bunk?

13:36.982 --> 13:38.108
What are you saying?

13:38.776 --> 13:39.902
Are you scoping it out?

13:39.985 --> 13:41.821
How come you're staying
at the office in the first place?

13:42.404 --> 13:44.114
I have a good reason.

13:44.198 --> 13:45.741
Well, I do too.

13:49.495 --> 13:52.248
Oh, I like this.

13:58.337 --> 13:59.713
I'll be waiting out front.

14:00.631 --> 14:01.590
I'm coming.

14:02.132 --> 14:04.301
Hurry. I have so much to get done today.

14:04.385 --> 14:07.012
I'm going to have to swing by the office
for training this morning.

14:07.096 --> 14:08.639
Okay? And then, three open houses.

14:08.722 --> 14:09.849
So you'll be home late?

14:09.932 --> 14:11.684
You can have dinner for yourself.

14:11.767 --> 14:14.937
- There's rice in the rice cooker.
- And the sides are in the fridge.

14:15.020 --> 14:18.190
- I'll just take them out and eat.
- Oh, a little adult, aren't you?

14:23.779 --> 14:24.989
Is it Dad's?

14:25.573 --> 14:26.907
Why did he leave this?

14:26.991 --> 14:29.201
He does whatever he wants in the moment.

14:29.285 --> 14:31.579
I don't get why he'd come home,
then leave.

14:36.542 --> 14:39.587
Your Pop was never good
at throwing stuff away.

14:40.754 --> 14:43.132
It's hard for me to get rid
of all these old things

14:43.215 --> 14:45.050
that he brings home here to me.

14:45.634 --> 14:46.886
Go ahead, if you want.

14:47.553 --> 14:48.470
Huh?

14:48.554 --> 14:49.847
Divorce.

14:50.681 --> 14:51.599
What?

14:51.682 --> 14:53.058
I'd survive it now.

14:56.145 --> 14:57.062
Bo-mi?

14:58.314 --> 14:59.982
You can't just say stuff like that.

15:00.482 --> 15:01.400
Bo-mi!

15:05.279 --> 15:06.989
Bo-mi.

15:07.072 --> 15:09.533
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

15:11.368 --> 15:13.913
- You're here early.
- Why were you in there?

15:14.622 --> 15:17.541
Uh… I had something to do.

15:17.625 --> 15:18.626
Hmm.

15:23.213 --> 15:24.214
And yesterday?

15:24.298 --> 15:26.091
I had some things to take care of.

15:27.509 --> 15:28.469
Why?

15:29.053 --> 15:32.640
Oh, I was just wondering
because you didn't call or…

15:34.725 --> 15:36.143
You were waiting for a call?

15:36.894 --> 15:37.728
No.

15:38.646 --> 15:39.772
You were, though.

15:39.855 --> 15:41.190
No, I was not, really.

15:50.074 --> 15:51.659
What are you doing? We're at work.

15:53.285 --> 15:54.495
You were waiting.

15:54.578 --> 15:56.163
I could see it on your face.

15:58.123 --> 16:00.250
I guess you haven't heard, Forecaster.

16:00.334 --> 16:03.003
I'm kinda famous in the KMA
for my poker face.

16:03.087 --> 16:04.254
Also, how do they say it?

16:04.338 --> 16:06.632
I was born to put up walls
or something like that.

16:06.715 --> 16:08.926
- Who said that?
- I did.

16:09.009 --> 16:11.762
You've got a gift
for self-analysis, really.

16:13.138 --> 16:15.140
You're getting too familiar, okay?

16:15.224 --> 16:17.601
Just, um, professional friendliness.

16:18.102 --> 16:19.645
I don't know why a forecaster

16:19.728 --> 16:21.438
would need to be friendly
with his director.

16:21.522 --> 16:23.524
- Well, we're special.
- What's so--

16:24.108 --> 16:25.275
Good morning.

16:25.359 --> 16:27.152
- Good morning!
- Hello, Assistant Director.

16:33.450 --> 16:34.410
Let's go.

16:38.414 --> 16:39.832
Hello, and good morning.

16:44.753 --> 16:46.672
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

16:48.632 --> 16:50.134
- Doors closing.
- Oh, wait, hold the door.

16:50.217 --> 16:52.302
Please hold the door. Please.
Please. Thanks.

16:53.387 --> 16:54.346
Hello.

16:54.430 --> 16:56.265
Oh, um, thank you.

16:57.266 --> 16:58.559
Doors closing.

17:01.103 --> 17:04.356
I saw your husband register
for leave of absence?

17:05.315 --> 17:09.361
Oh, when I was in Disaster Prevention,
he was my advisor.

17:09.445 --> 17:11.530
Ah.

17:11.613 --> 17:13.741
He's not unwell or anything, is he?

17:13.824 --> 17:15.200
Ah, nothing like that.

17:15.284 --> 17:18.454
He wants to study for something,
so I said he should take a year off.

17:18.537 --> 17:19.913
What about your household?

17:19.997 --> 17:21.415
Well, I've got it.

17:21.999 --> 17:23.167
Oh, wow.

17:23.250 --> 17:25.502
Isn't your younger son
just starting elementary school?

17:25.586 --> 17:27.296
Won't it be hard if you're the only…

17:27.880 --> 17:31.592
Well, we're married
and we both are there for the other.

17:31.675 --> 17:33.052
Doors opening.

17:37.890 --> 17:39.224
Isn't this your floor?

17:42.519 --> 17:43.896
Doors closing.

17:51.695 --> 17:53.655
Oh, thanks.

17:54.156 --> 17:55.407
Here you go.

18:00.370 --> 18:02.289
Is something going on?

18:02.873 --> 18:04.083
Oh, the thing is…

18:04.583 --> 18:07.002
I have a friend
who got married not long ago.

18:08.170 --> 18:09.213
Ah.

18:11.673 --> 18:12.633
Okay, so?

18:12.716 --> 18:13.926
He did the whole wedding

18:14.009 --> 18:18.180
even though everyone told him not to
'cause he was sure he loved her.

18:18.263 --> 18:19.139
Okay.

18:19.223 --> 18:20.307
So they had their wedding,

18:20.390 --> 18:23.310
saw the whole thing through,
and now they won't agree to register it.

18:24.103 --> 18:25.687
Your friend or his wife?

18:25.771 --> 18:27.231
Wife, of course.

18:27.314 --> 18:28.774
What do you think she's thinking?

18:28.857 --> 18:31.193
Oh, well…

18:31.693 --> 18:33.445
I do understand.

18:34.655 --> 18:36.156
You understand her?

18:36.240 --> 18:37.407
Mm-hmm.

18:37.491 --> 18:40.285
She could have conceivably jumped
into this wedding out of impulse.

18:40.369 --> 18:43.872
However, ultimately,
when they finally came to register,

18:44.873 --> 18:46.917
she finally started to see things clearly.

18:48.127 --> 18:49.128
Oh.

18:49.920 --> 18:53.257
Then, is she regretting doing it now?

18:53.340 --> 18:54.758
Or it could be…

18:55.342 --> 18:56.718
she suddenly was scared.

18:56.802 --> 18:58.011
Hmm?

18:59.555 --> 19:02.558
I think, sometimes,
when it's not just the heart,

19:02.641 --> 19:06.019
but actually the law,
it feels like you're crossing a line

19:06.103 --> 19:08.981
where you can never again
go back to the other side.

19:13.443 --> 19:15.195
Possibly this wife of his

19:15.863 --> 19:18.574
is unsure about the marriage
in the first place.

19:19.074 --> 19:20.784
Love is trusting together.

19:22.244 --> 19:25.998
They say that where there's trust,
courage will appear also.

19:26.832 --> 19:31.044
The courage to go through anything
if it's along with the one you love, okay?

19:44.099 --> 19:47.227
- How is the atmosphere?
- Hmm, the upper level trough

19:47.311 --> 19:48.854
is slowly moving on to the East Sea,

19:48.937 --> 19:52.441
so the flow of the anticyclone of Korea
is going to be slow for a while.

19:52.524 --> 19:54.193
And solar radiation's going up.

19:55.152 --> 19:57.237
And the concentration
of ozone will rise as well.

19:57.946 --> 20:01.366
It might get all the way
to the warning level by noon.

20:02.034 --> 20:06.038
Oh, great. The phones are all
gonna start ringing off the hook today.

20:06.663 --> 20:08.290
Call to the Air Quality
Forecasting Center.

20:08.373 --> 20:09.499
Sure.

20:10.500 --> 20:14.546
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

20:25.390 --> 20:27.017
It's ironic, isn't it?

20:27.100 --> 20:28.268
Hmm? What?

20:29.353 --> 20:30.437
Ozone, I mean.

20:31.396 --> 20:34.816
It's really helpful
when it's in the stratosphere.

20:35.859 --> 20:38.320
But it's a hazard when it gets too close.

20:40.280 --> 20:42.866
Well, there's an optimal distance
for everything.

20:43.617 --> 20:45.744
At least we can calculate
the ideal distance

20:45.827 --> 20:47.579
between ozone and humans.

20:48.330 --> 20:51.041
Other boundaries
are impossible to figure out.

20:51.625 --> 20:52.960
Oh? What, for example?

20:53.043 --> 20:55.462
Like for two people, you know, it's…

20:57.589 --> 21:00.300
There's no way of knowing
until you just confront it.

21:02.511 --> 21:06.390
I heard once that hedgehogs
poke each other a thousand times

21:06.473 --> 21:09.393
before they figure out how close
they can get without hurting each other.

21:10.769 --> 21:12.104
You can't avoid hurting each other

21:12.187 --> 21:15.107
in the process of figuring out
how close you can get.

21:15.190 --> 21:16.233
That's right.

21:17.276 --> 21:21.905
Well, there's people who have been trying
to work it out for over a decade.

21:22.489 --> 21:23.365
Like I am.

21:26.660 --> 21:28.078
Did you go back home?

21:29.121 --> 21:30.080
No.

21:30.163 --> 21:32.165
I was away too long, I think.

21:32.749 --> 21:37.796
And now, the optimal distance
between me and my family is pretty far.

21:38.338 --> 21:40.674
Maybe it's best to just see them
once in a while,

21:41.300 --> 21:43.802
the way we're doing it right now.

21:44.303 --> 21:46.680
Oh, no. That's a poor excuse.

21:47.264 --> 21:48.307
You think so?

21:55.439 --> 21:57.566
The rainfall probability
is low today, right?

21:59.359 --> 22:02.154
Right. It's lower than 20 percent.

22:02.863 --> 22:04.531
Okay. Mm, thanks.

22:05.282 --> 22:10.996
Everyone, today we can expect to have
over a 0.3ppm ozone concentration.

22:11.580 --> 22:14.166
The Air Quality Forecasting Center
will keep calling us

22:14.249 --> 22:17.461
to check on solar radiation
and cloud coverage, so be cooperative.

22:17.544 --> 22:21.423
Please respond quickly and politely
to ozone situation increase, all right?

22:21.506 --> 22:22.799
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

22:25.218 --> 22:26.428
I can't do that.

22:26.511 --> 22:27.721
You know dealing with the press

22:27.804 --> 22:30.057
is already more than enough work
during monsoon season.

22:30.640 --> 22:32.392
Plus, I'm writing a column every month.

22:32.476 --> 22:34.061
How can I write a feature article too?

22:34.144 --> 22:37.731
I'm aware. That's why I told him
that it might not happen.

22:38.357 --> 22:41.318
But I do think they're gonna bug
Reporter Chae about this.

22:41.401 --> 22:42.986
I'm talking about your wife.

22:43.070 --> 22:44.154
Sorry?

22:44.237 --> 22:46.865
Their chief editor
asked for you specifically.

22:47.491 --> 22:50.994
They asked if Deputy Director Han Ki-jun
was Chae Yu-jin's husband.

22:54.373 --> 22:56.958
Let's just see what's…
what's really going on here.

22:59.002 --> 22:59.920
Huh?

23:00.670 --> 23:01.922
A feature article?

23:02.881 --> 23:06.009
Isn't your husband a spokesman at the KMA?

23:06.093 --> 23:08.553
The guy on TV
whenever there's a weather alert.

23:10.305 --> 23:11.348
Yeah.

23:11.431 --> 23:12.974
And he's such a great writer.

23:13.558 --> 23:16.853
I always read his magazine column.
"Ozone High and Low."

23:16.937 --> 23:19.106
Right? That's your husband?

23:20.774 --> 23:21.942
Yes.

23:22.025 --> 23:24.361
Could you ask him to use that talent

23:24.444 --> 23:26.279
to write us a new feature article
on weather?

23:27.406 --> 23:29.699
- Okay?
- Oh…

23:34.663 --> 23:37.165
KI-JUN

23:42.212 --> 23:44.172
KI-JUN

23:52.681 --> 23:54.182
Oppa, what's going on?

23:54.266 --> 23:57.310
- Hey, you busy?
- No, not really.

23:57.894 --> 24:00.230
Why? Why are you calling?

24:00.313 --> 24:02.607
Well, I don't need a reason to call you.

24:02.691 --> 24:04.818
I just wanted to hear your sweet voice.

24:06.987 --> 24:07.904
So everything's good?

24:13.952 --> 24:17.414
Yeah. Of… of course, yeah.

24:17.497 --> 24:19.082
Ah, I see.

24:20.500 --> 24:21.585
Okay, then.

24:22.294 --> 24:24.045
You can go back to work.
I'll see you at home.

24:24.129 --> 24:26.298
Oh, uh, okay.

24:42.105 --> 24:44.941
- Kim Soo-jin from Team Two here.
- Is this the weather authority?

24:45.025 --> 24:47.861
How can you slap us
with an ozone warning out of nowhere?

24:48.487 --> 24:50.197
My preschooler's got a field trip today.

24:50.280 --> 24:52.949
I took a whole day off of work
to chaperone for her.

24:53.658 --> 24:55.911
I mean, you should at least
give us one day of warning.

24:55.994 --> 24:58.955
Of course. Ozone levels
can increase very suddenly

24:59.039 --> 25:00.999
because of car exhausts
and other air pollutants.

25:01.082 --> 25:03.210
The warnings go out as soon as we know.

25:03.293 --> 25:06.588
Also, we're not the ones
who send the alert to the public.

25:06.671 --> 25:08.423
Don't be ridiculous. Hey!

25:08.507 --> 25:11.426
The weather is perfectly fine.
What's with the ozone warning?

25:11.510 --> 25:13.011
They're telling all of us, truckers,

25:13.094 --> 25:15.805
that our cargo trucks won't be allowed
into the metro area.

25:15.889 --> 25:17.557
Are you gonna pay for our delays?

25:17.641 --> 25:21.186
Okay, listen, sir. There's never
a good reason to be rude.

25:21.269 --> 25:24.147
Talk to the Environmental Ministry
or the Road Authority about it.

25:24.231 --> 25:27.108
Our office is not responsible
for the actual warning.

25:27.192 --> 25:29.361
But isn't ozone a good thing, though?

25:29.444 --> 25:31.154
Something like we need an ozone layer.

25:31.238 --> 25:33.490
Yes, that's right,
when it's in the stratosphere.

25:33.573 --> 25:36.535
It's harmful to the human body
when there's too much near the surface.

25:36.618 --> 25:39.120
Oh, I see. Hmm.

25:39.204 --> 25:44.417
By the way, how old are you, miss?
You sound cute. You single?

25:45.293 --> 25:46.461
Goodbye.

25:55.095 --> 25:57.180
I can get it. Go and get some food.

25:57.264 --> 25:59.099
I got them. I'm really okay.

25:59.182 --> 26:00.517
You can do this later.

26:01.142 --> 26:03.228
I'm not hungry.

26:04.145 --> 26:06.439
Hello, this is Kim Soo-jin with Team Two.

26:08.108 --> 26:11.820
Yes. But ozone warnings
are not the KMA's responsibility.

26:11.903 --> 26:13.863
Oh, hello, sir.

26:13.947 --> 26:15.365
- Hey.
- Hello.

26:15.448 --> 26:16.324
Hmm.

26:17.158 --> 26:18.159
Where is Director Jin?

26:18.243 --> 26:21.204
Uh, Policy Division
to talk about the post-analysis.

26:21.288 --> 26:22.289
Oh, I see.

26:22.956 --> 26:24.958
- Uh, carry on. Carry on.
- Yes, sir.

26:27.294 --> 26:28.336
Keep it up.

26:29.504 --> 26:31.089
- Oh, Mr. Um.
- Yes?

26:32.048 --> 26:34.134
Let's grab a coffee. Come on.

26:43.768 --> 26:44.644
Sir, please.

26:44.728 --> 26:46.146
Please just stop shouting.

26:46.646 --> 26:48.815
What? Shouting?

26:49.316 --> 26:51.568
I think you're confused. I did not shout.

26:51.651 --> 26:52.736
You did, sir.

26:52.819 --> 26:55.447
You've been shouting at me
ever since we started our call.

26:55.947 --> 26:57.616
Why you… Hey!

26:57.699 --> 27:00.744
Do you want to get suspended?
Who do you think you're talking to?

27:00.827 --> 27:03.038
I could make you write me
an apology letter.

27:03.121 --> 27:04.789
Hey!

27:04.873 --> 27:07.000
My son is a high-ranking public official.

27:07.083 --> 27:10.420
One word to him and your career is over.
You get me, sweetheart?

27:11.671 --> 27:12.756
Good afternoon, sir.

27:12.839 --> 27:14.924
If your son's so great, maybe you can go

27:15.008 --> 27:18.553
and complain about the weather to him
instead of just calling us about it.

27:19.137 --> 27:22.515
Also, ozone warnings
are not under the KMA's jurisdiction.

27:22.599 --> 27:26.061
They're the Ministry of Environment's.
How can we make that more clear?

27:26.144 --> 27:29.564
If you wanna yell at someone,
yell at them. I don't care. Good day!

27:41.493 --> 27:42.952
Can we do that?

27:43.536 --> 27:45.789
No, we can't… But…

27:47.207 --> 27:48.458
we're human beings.

27:49.542 --> 27:52.879
We have the right to defend ourselves
if abuse is thrown at us.

27:52.962 --> 27:54.047
I don't know.

27:56.007 --> 27:59.010
It's fine, Ms. Kim. Don't worry.

27:59.094 --> 28:00.553
I'll handle the follow-up.

28:25.578 --> 28:27.455
Oh, where
are you going, Forecaster?

28:27.539 --> 28:30.750
Oh, I have something to take care of.

28:30.834 --> 28:33.837
See you.

28:39.968 --> 28:40.927
Sorry?

28:41.553 --> 28:43.012
Ten mil and 600K?

28:44.347 --> 28:45.932
And maintenance expenses too?

28:47.517 --> 28:48.643
Um…

28:49.728 --> 28:53.690
What about 500,000
including the maintenance costs?

28:53.773 --> 28:55.567
I told you I can't do that.

28:55.650 --> 28:58.236
For 500,000, the place
you saw yesterday was the best option.

28:58.319 --> 29:01.364
Could you ask the building owner
about it just once more?

29:01.448 --> 29:03.450
I'm a very, very good tenant.

29:03.533 --> 29:05.994
And I'll basically only be there
to sleep, no more.

29:06.077 --> 29:08.580
I mean, we already know
what their answer is.

29:09.456 --> 29:11.708
I would really appreciate it
so much, ma'am.

29:11.791 --> 29:12.876
Thank you.

29:15.044 --> 29:16.546
Yes, I understand.

29:18.256 --> 29:19.841
I'm aware of the situation.

29:22.469 --> 29:25.930
Did you come all the way to Headquarters
just to act like some sad widower?

29:26.431 --> 29:27.682
What are you talking about?

29:27.766 --> 29:30.685
I'm not a widower.
I have my wife and my daughter.

29:31.770 --> 29:34.773
I know you do.
You have a home, a wife, and a kid.

29:34.856 --> 29:37.358
So why are you crashing here for free
like you're homeless?

29:38.276 --> 29:40.153
The weather alerts are serious right now.

29:40.236 --> 29:42.572
Back in the day, we used
to almost live in the building

29:42.655 --> 29:44.574
during the worst of the monsoon season.

29:44.657 --> 29:45.700
So, uh, what's wrong?

29:45.784 --> 29:48.870
That's right. That was when we
didn't have a central server here, man.

29:50.079 --> 29:51.456
Why would you need to do that now

29:51.539 --> 29:54.083
when you could be in bed and look
at the charts all the way to China?

29:54.918 --> 29:55.919
Anyway…

29:56.419 --> 29:58.213
All the young people

29:58.296 --> 29:59.881
hate that you're doing this.

29:59.964 --> 30:02.050
What do you mean by "the young people"?

30:02.592 --> 30:05.178
Lots of them wanna use
the night-duty room sometimes.

30:05.762 --> 30:08.681
They all think it's weird
that you're basically living in there.

30:08.765 --> 30:11.893
I got a whole stack
of complaints this high, okay?

30:11.976 --> 30:14.479
Uh-huh.

30:15.522 --> 30:17.398
Pack up and get your stuff out of there.

30:18.483 --> 30:21.611
You took a pay cut to come to Headquarters
so you could be closer to your family.

30:22.195 --> 30:23.571
That's the only reason you're here.

30:23.655 --> 30:26.407
You could have just stayed
at the top of the Gangwon Office,

30:26.491 --> 30:28.284
- and you'd have been set.
- Ah, people in Seoul

30:28.368 --> 30:30.036
are too cold-hearted for me, okay?

30:30.119 --> 30:32.997
Does your wife know
that you're just moping around over here?

30:34.624 --> 30:37.001
She told me to do whatever I want.

30:41.589 --> 30:42.465
Well, you do that.

30:44.384 --> 30:48.012
A talent for knowing the winds
of the east wind is no good if, uh…

30:48.555 --> 30:50.473
if you can't even get a read
on your own wife.

30:51.057 --> 30:51.975
Here, toss this for me.

31:16.791 --> 31:18.585
Who was handling
the complaint calls

31:18.668 --> 31:20.128
that came in to Team Two today?

31:20.920 --> 31:22.088
I was.

31:23.798 --> 31:24.799
What's this about?

31:25.383 --> 31:27.385
Your Bureau has received
a conduct warning.

31:29.012 --> 31:31.723
I heard you scolded someone
who called out the ozone warning

31:31.806 --> 31:34.475
for asking about things
outside KMA jurisdiction.

31:36.644 --> 31:39.063
Believe me. I know it's hard
to deal with complaint calls,

31:39.147 --> 31:41.274
but you can't just tell them off
and then hang up.

31:43.443 --> 31:45.361
Is this the truth, Ms. Kim?

31:46.487 --> 31:47.822
Um, uh…

31:47.906 --> 31:48.865
I did it.

31:50.533 --> 31:52.869
This is not the time
to cover for her, Assistant Director.

31:52.952 --> 31:54.329
I'm not covering anything.

31:54.412 --> 31:55.955
I took the call.

31:57.498 --> 31:58.625
Look what happens.

31:59.125 --> 32:01.210
Take responsibility
for your own failings, and look.

32:01.294 --> 32:03.671
Is this something that she
should have to take the blame for?

32:03.755 --> 32:05.798
What are you saying, Deputy Director Han?

32:05.882 --> 32:09.719
I took the call. I was on the call.
I yelled at the caller.

32:09.802 --> 32:11.763
It wasn't her. Are we clear?

32:15.141 --> 32:16.935
You should have restrained yourself.

32:17.018 --> 32:18.186
That was not an option.

32:18.269 --> 32:19.896
He was bragging he can get us all fired.

32:19.979 --> 32:21.439
What am I supposed to say to that?

32:21.940 --> 32:24.525
That's not a complaint, sir.
That's abusive.

32:24.609 --> 32:27.612
We're not some kind of trash can
they can just throw their anger in.

32:27.695 --> 32:31.032
We don't have to just sit there
and deal with that kind of crap.

32:33.076 --> 32:34.202
All right, then.

32:35.119 --> 32:38.331
Anyway, try to do a better job, Ms. Kim.

32:40.375 --> 32:42.961
Why would you let Mrs. Oh
take your calls and create this mess?

32:43.044 --> 32:45.797
This whole thing went down
'cause you couldn't handle your job.

32:45.880 --> 32:46.839
Wouldn't you say?

32:46.923 --> 32:48.675
Deputy Director Han, that's enough.

32:48.758 --> 32:50.343
It's all too much to take.

32:52.595 --> 32:54.180
What was I supposed to do

32:54.263 --> 32:56.766
when the first thing he said was,
"Do you know who my son is?"

32:57.600 --> 32:58.893
That's not all.

32:58.977 --> 33:00.561
Every one of these people is so rude.

33:00.645 --> 33:02.814
They all ask this weird stuff
like if I'm married.

33:02.897 --> 33:04.816
Plus they say I'm a dumb brat.

33:08.569 --> 33:10.905
Uh…

33:10.989 --> 33:15.201
I'm here at the KMA
because I wanted to forecast weather.

33:15.284 --> 33:17.161
I didn't do all that work in school

33:17.245 --> 33:19.372
only to come here
and work in a call center.

33:25.461 --> 33:26.963
Do-don't…

33:27.046 --> 33:30.633
I'll write a report on this,
following the proper procedure.

33:31.342 --> 33:32.301
You can go now.

33:32.385 --> 33:33.970
Oh, uh, um…

33:34.554 --> 33:36.222
Uh, all right.

33:52.989 --> 33:54.240
Ms. Kim.

33:54.824 --> 33:55.783
Yes?

33:56.659 --> 33:59.037
We are here to do that kind of work.

34:03.124 --> 34:05.209
What are you saying right now, Director?

34:07.211 --> 34:13.259
I know it's hard to listen
to the callers and their… complaints.

34:13.342 --> 34:19.432
It's crazy to see how many people's lives
are affected by some… ozone warning, huh?

34:23.186 --> 34:25.646
Cargo truck drivers
whose lives are at stake,

34:25.730 --> 34:27.231
children who can't play outside,

34:27.315 --> 34:30.151
and people who don't even know
what ozone warnings mean.

34:30.234 --> 34:34.113
If we didn't have to hear out
every one of these people's complaints,

34:34.197 --> 34:36.199
could we have known, hmm?

34:38.326 --> 34:39.702
Could we have understood

34:39.786 --> 34:42.955
who our forecasts affect
and the ways they're affected?

34:46.542 --> 34:49.045
We all studied hard to pass
the civil service exam

34:49.128 --> 34:50.379
and be where we are right now.

34:50.963 --> 34:53.424
So we can serve the people
and protect them too.

34:55.009 --> 34:58.679
So listen. We're not just a call center.

34:58.763 --> 35:00.556
Our jobs here are crucial.

35:00.640 --> 35:01.724
Do you understand?

35:15.738 --> 35:16.781
Are you okay?

35:19.450 --> 35:20.660
You did good.

35:29.961 --> 35:33.673
I didn't study hard
to pass the civil service exam

35:33.756 --> 35:36.759
just so I could sit here
and take calls from rude strangers.

35:36.843 --> 35:39.554
Why do I have to put up
with this kind of treatment now?

35:42.056 --> 35:45.935
Why do you think we're all here
after all of our studying?

35:48.104 --> 35:51.107
It's so we can serve the public interest.

35:51.190 --> 35:53.860
To make sure we do our best every day.

35:53.943 --> 35:55.945
That's why the taxpayers pay our salaries.

35:56.028 --> 35:58.239
You thought this was some easy stable job?

35:58.322 --> 35:59.448
Well, it isn't.

35:59.532 --> 36:02.410
You should find a new line of work,
if that's what you're after.

36:02.493 --> 36:06.080
You can't work here if you don't have
a sense of duty and responsibility.

36:06.164 --> 36:07.123
Understand?

36:09.333 --> 36:10.251
Yes, sir.

36:21.137 --> 36:22.680
She's grown, huh?

36:25.683 --> 36:26.767
Cheer up.

36:26.851 --> 36:30.271
I'm sorry that you got scolded
for something I did, too.

36:31.189 --> 36:33.024
Well, it didn't feel like a scolding.

36:33.941 --> 36:36.736
It actually hit me square in the skull.

36:38.988 --> 36:41.532
While I was answering phone calls
from rude people all day long,

36:41.616 --> 36:44.410
I thought, "What's my real purpose here?"

36:44.994 --> 36:48.706
But what Director Jin said to me
showed me purpose.

36:48.789 --> 36:50.708
Are you serious?

36:50.791 --> 36:53.127
Our Kim Soo-jin's all grown up now.

36:54.253 --> 36:56.005
These are the moments
where you grow as a person.

36:56.088 --> 36:59.884
Even Jin Ha-kyung
wasn't born like that, right?

36:59.967 --> 37:02.345
Anyway, see you.

37:02.428 --> 37:03.971
- See you all later, okay?
- Oh.

37:04.055 --> 37:05.056
- Goodbye.
- Good night, sir.

37:05.139 --> 37:06.474
Good night. See you.

37:09.477 --> 37:11.896
I guess he's going to sleep
down there again.

37:12.688 --> 37:14.106
He was away for too long.

37:14.190 --> 37:16.567
Home can be difficult for him.

37:17.151 --> 37:18.527
Doors opening.

37:18.611 --> 37:19.695
Hello.

37:19.779 --> 37:20.821
- Hello.
- Hello.

37:23.157 --> 37:24.283
You're going?

37:24.367 --> 37:26.410
Oh, go ahead, really.
I'm gonna take the next one down.

37:27.286 --> 37:28.996
- See you tomorrow, Forecaster.
- Good night.

37:29.080 --> 37:30.414
Doors closing.

37:31.958 --> 37:33.334
Doors opening.

37:35.169 --> 37:38.172
Oh, please go ahead.

37:38.256 --> 37:39.882
- Okay.
- Yeah.

37:41.801 --> 37:43.135
Doors closing.

37:53.479 --> 37:55.982
Doors opening.

38:00.528 --> 38:01.779
Oh, please go ahead.

38:01.862 --> 38:03.406
- Doors closing.
- Bye.

38:41.193 --> 38:42.611
What are you doing here?

38:42.695 --> 38:46.365
Oh, the elevator was full.
So I was waiting for the next one.

38:46.449 --> 38:47.325
Mm.

38:48.200 --> 38:50.411
I'm hungry. Wanna get food now?

38:53.039 --> 38:54.206
Naengsam?

38:54.290 --> 38:55.207
Sure.

38:56.125 --> 38:57.877
CHILDREN'S BOOKS
BEST SELLERS AND NEW RELEASES

39:12.141 --> 39:14.185
Is this the book
that you were looking for?

39:14.268 --> 39:15.811
Yes, it is. Thank you.

39:16.354 --> 39:18.773
Where was it, though?
I was looking all over.

39:18.856 --> 39:21.859
Oh, yes. It was buried down in storage.

39:22.943 --> 39:24.153
"Storage"?

39:24.236 --> 39:26.447
Checkout is over there. Thank you.

39:26.530 --> 39:27.531
Thanks.

39:30.743 --> 39:33.621
CITY ALLIGATOR
BY JIN TAE-KYUNG

40:18.374 --> 40:20.876
- Looking for this one?
- No, no. Go ahead.

40:26.757 --> 40:27.675
Aren't you…

40:30.719 --> 40:33.264
Oh, you recognize me?

40:34.515 --> 40:36.851
Well, oh, yes, I did…

40:37.977 --> 40:39.353
The side dish girl, right?

40:39.854 --> 40:41.355
"Side dishes"?

40:42.314 --> 40:46.193
You gave me those side dishes
to keep for your sister, Ms. 1201.

40:46.277 --> 40:47.361
Oh…

40:47.445 --> 40:48.988
Mr. 1302?

40:52.032 --> 40:54.869
Why hasn't she gone to get them? It's…

40:58.122 --> 40:59.957
She's not answering her phone.

41:07.173 --> 41:09.884
Please tell your sister
that I'm going to throw

41:09.967 --> 41:12.970
every last one of them away
if she doesn't get them by tomorrow.

41:14.138 --> 41:15.222
Oh, just wait a second.

41:16.432 --> 41:17.641
You can't go yet.

41:19.018 --> 41:19.935
Why?

41:20.519 --> 41:24.190
Uh, that book you were reading,
City Alligator,

41:24.273 --> 41:28.486
please tell me which part made you laugh
like you were laughing.

41:28.569 --> 41:29.570
Ah…

41:30.696 --> 41:33.240
I didn't laugh because it was funny.

41:33.324 --> 41:34.533
Why, then?

41:35.743 --> 41:37.495
I just had the thought that the only way

41:37.578 --> 41:39.914
an alligator goes to
a city is if it's a purse.

41:40.998 --> 41:42.416
I mean, they're reptiles, right?

41:42.500 --> 41:43.459
They live in water.

41:43.542 --> 41:46.253
So it's not exactly like
they can just go and live in the city.

41:46.337 --> 41:48.339
Yet the book was called City Alligator.

41:48.422 --> 41:52.092
Couldn't one call that poetic license?

41:53.761 --> 41:55.095
Let me tell you something.

41:55.179 --> 41:56.889
The person who wrote that book,

41:56.972 --> 41:59.141
I doubt they even looked up
alligators online.

41:59.225 --> 42:01.769
Let alone do any serious research
on the subject.

42:01.852 --> 42:02.978
I don't think that's true.

42:03.062 --> 42:04.396
If they did, they would have known

42:04.480 --> 42:07.441
that the toes on an alligator's hind feet
and forefeet are different.

42:08.609 --> 42:09.735
Toes on their…

42:10.319 --> 42:14.490
The thing about alligators is they
all have five toes on their front feet

42:14.573 --> 42:15.950
and in the back, just four.

42:16.784 --> 42:18.202
But in that book…

42:19.245 --> 42:21.163
Jeez, well…

42:22.206 --> 42:25.543
It's really true these days that writer
just means you picked up a pen.

42:25.626 --> 42:27.920
Still, that author lacked even the basics.

42:28.003 --> 42:30.005
I was laughing
'cause I thought it was sad.

42:32.550 --> 42:35.261
- I'm sorry I lack the basics.
- Huh?

42:40.307 --> 42:42.518
Are you actually…

42:47.356 --> 42:48.274
Uh…

43:01.120 --> 43:03.289
- This is done too.
- Thank you.

43:22.516 --> 43:23.475
Who is it?

43:23.559 --> 43:25.686
Hmm. Oh, it's no one.

43:26.895 --> 43:28.022
Is it good?

43:36.822 --> 43:38.782
Did I come on too strong earlier?

43:38.866 --> 43:39.908
What… what do you mean?

43:41.160 --> 43:42.286
Mm…

43:42.953 --> 43:45.080
I thought that
when I said we should move in,

43:45.164 --> 43:46.415
maybe that was too much.

43:47.750 --> 43:50.628
No. I like that you were being honest.

43:50.711 --> 43:53.505
It made me wanna tell you
my honest opinion as well.

43:55.758 --> 43:59.720
I feel like it's been a little awkward,
now that I brought it up.

43:59.803 --> 44:02.640
I felt like there's sort of a distance
between the two of us.

44:04.183 --> 44:07.186
Isn't that distance what you wanted?

44:07.269 --> 44:08.729
I mean to keep us a secret?

44:08.812 --> 44:11.649
Obviously, I didn't mean
to keep secrets from each other.

44:13.942 --> 44:17.571
Is this 'cause I didn't tell you
who that text was from?

44:19.073 --> 44:20.991
Mm, well, that's part of it. Mm-hmm.

44:28.582 --> 44:29.625
Then here.

44:32.419 --> 44:33.379
A realtor?

44:33.879 --> 44:35.714
Yeah, a realtor.

44:35.798 --> 44:36.965
And the new tour.

44:37.549 --> 44:38.634
What is this for?

44:38.717 --> 44:40.719
I can't stay
at the training center forever.

44:43.013 --> 44:45.724
I knew that it's hard
to find a place in Seoul,

44:45.808 --> 44:47.559
but it's even harder than I thought.

44:48.143 --> 44:51.188
Yesterday, I was running around
all day, all for nothing.

44:52.147 --> 44:54.233
Is, um… Is this what you meant

44:54.316 --> 44:56.151
when you said
you had something to do yesterday?

44:56.235 --> 44:57.236
Yeah.

44:59.363 --> 45:02.116
Si-woo, I'm asking
because I'm genuinely curious.

45:02.199 --> 45:05.160
Why are you going
out of your way to do this

45:05.244 --> 45:07.371
when it would be so much easier
to move in with me?

45:08.330 --> 45:09.623
Mm, it's because

45:10.374 --> 45:14.128
I believe someone should keep
their love and private lives separate.

45:18.841 --> 45:20.676
Are you sure it's not about your ego?

45:23.721 --> 45:26.890
Director, I can't be honest with you
if you try to get under my skin.

45:28.308 --> 45:31.270
Honestly, I'm not proud
of my current situation, okay?

45:31.895 --> 45:34.356
But I'm not ashamed of it either.

45:39.153 --> 45:41.071
What? What are you…

45:42.197 --> 45:43.574
It's nothing.

45:49.955 --> 45:51.999
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

45:53.625 --> 45:55.335
Can we also have one bottle of soju?

45:55.419 --> 45:56.503
Yes.

46:23.363 --> 46:25.616
- What are you doing?
- Goddamn it!

46:32.456 --> 46:33.916
I just asked.

46:35.876 --> 46:36.835
Damn it.

46:37.753 --> 46:39.922
Ah!

46:47.888 --> 46:48.931
Uh, what are…

46:50.766 --> 46:52.851
Are you hungry? Go and sit.

46:59.775 --> 47:01.860
Thank you for this.

47:02.611 --> 47:03.612
Mm-hmm.

47:20.754 --> 47:21.630
Uh, what's this?

47:21.713 --> 47:23.465
CREDIT LOANS
FOR FULL-TIME CIVIL SERVANTS

47:23.549 --> 47:25.926
Well, I thought we could pay
our deposit with a loan.

47:26.009 --> 47:28.053
Of course, this also puts us in debt.

47:28.136 --> 47:32.140
But the interest on this one is way better
than a home loan if you're newlyweds.

47:42.192 --> 47:45.279
I heard that your chief editor
asked if I could write a column.

47:45.362 --> 47:46.530
Where did you hear that?

47:47.197 --> 47:49.700
You really should have told me
about something like that.

47:51.451 --> 47:52.870
I know you're real busy.

47:53.579 --> 47:56.623
I just really didn't want
to add to your stress.

47:57.708 --> 48:00.002
Tell him your oppa is gonna do it.

48:01.378 --> 48:02.212
Serious?

48:02.296 --> 48:03.547
Mm-hmm.

48:03.630 --> 48:07.926
If I don't do it, then your chief editor
is gonna give you a hard time about it.

48:08.010 --> 48:10.888
And people will think that you can't get
your husband to do anything.

48:10.971 --> 48:12.514
Are you sure you have time, though?

48:13.307 --> 48:15.309
I'll do it even if I don't have the time.

48:15.392 --> 48:17.102
You're my wife, after all.

48:18.312 --> 48:21.106
Okay, but serious,
I'm gonna tell him tomorrow, okay?

48:21.189 --> 48:22.482
Yeah, go ahead.

48:27.905 --> 48:29.615
By the way,
how did you find out about this?

48:30.866 --> 48:32.200
You're incredible.

48:35.621 --> 48:37.539
Love is trusting together.

48:37.623 --> 48:41.585
They say that where there's trust,
courage will appear also.

48:42.169 --> 48:46.423
The courage to go through anything
if it's along with the one you love, okay?

48:54.890 --> 48:56.975
- Did you do your homework?
- Yes.

48:58.185 --> 49:01.229
Mm, then today, addition of involutions.

49:02.064 --> 49:04.316
- Try to solve this and this first.
- Okay.

49:14.910 --> 49:18.580
What did you… mean
by what you said earlier?

49:19.164 --> 49:20.415
Hmm?

49:20.499 --> 49:23.669
Why would you say
I could divorce Dad if I want?

49:24.252 --> 49:25.212
You know.

49:26.755 --> 49:29.883
It seems like it's harder for you now
than it was when he was away.

49:30.509 --> 49:32.469
I just don't want you
going through that for me.

49:32.970 --> 49:34.471
I'm happy to live with Dad,

49:34.554 --> 49:36.932
but it's more important
to me that you are.

49:38.475 --> 49:41.478
No, I… I don't hate living with him.

49:42.354 --> 49:45.065
It's just… right now,

49:46.108 --> 49:48.402
your Pop and I just need
a little time alone.

49:48.986 --> 49:51.530
We've been apart for so long that…

49:52.823 --> 49:55.033
of course, we need
some time getting closer.

50:06.586 --> 50:08.338
Okay. I've finished, Ms. Lee.

50:09.965 --> 50:11.091
Ms. Lee?

50:11.174 --> 50:13.093
- Huh?
- Can you take a look at this?

50:13.844 --> 50:15.846
Oh, okay. Let's see.

50:46.043 --> 50:47.335
Dang it.

50:55.343 --> 50:56.887
FRIED CHICKEN

51:00.724 --> 51:02.434
- Here you go.
- Mm.

51:04.394 --> 51:06.354
Did you already have a drink somewhere?

51:06.438 --> 51:07.939
Yes, with my girlfriend.

51:08.648 --> 51:09.816
Just one.

51:11.151 --> 51:14.571
Why did you come here
and not to her place, then, huh?

51:15.238 --> 51:16.531
I, uh…

51:17.657 --> 51:20.285
I'm a little… I'm a little embarrassed.

51:20.994 --> 51:21.912
Why?

51:21.995 --> 51:25.749
To be honest, I don't have
a penny in the world.

51:25.832 --> 51:27.501
I've been holding out…

51:27.584 --> 51:30.837
with the one thing I do have,
and that's my pride.

51:33.131 --> 51:34.591
Well, I got busted tonight.

51:43.809 --> 51:45.310
Let me tell you a story.

51:47.979 --> 51:49.773
After my dad passed away,

51:51.775 --> 51:54.569
we were left with nothing,
not even a place to live.

51:57.572 --> 51:59.825
It was me, my sister, and my mom.

52:00.951 --> 52:03.745
The three of us had nowhere to go.

52:04.996 --> 52:07.999
We were hungry and it was so cold.

52:08.500 --> 52:10.919
Thinking that we might
have to stay outside all night,

52:11.419 --> 52:13.713
I just wanted to knock
on literally any door

52:13.797 --> 52:15.549
and ask if they could just let us stay.

52:15.632 --> 52:19.219
So, uh, what happened that night, then?

52:20.720 --> 52:22.305
We slept in the cold.

52:24.683 --> 52:27.644
The next day, my sister
went to live with my dad's older brother,

52:28.603 --> 52:30.897
and then I went
to my mom's younger sister.

52:30.981 --> 52:32.023
And Mom…

52:33.233 --> 52:34.776
got a job at a restaurant.

52:35.443 --> 52:37.654
So we had to live apart for a few years.

52:40.949 --> 52:44.786
So I understand what it's like
to have nowhere to go.

52:45.370 --> 52:48.165
And I also know how weary
your heart is right now.

52:50.667 --> 52:54.337
I respect you wanting to keep a line
between your love and your private life.

52:56.715 --> 52:58.216
And I also respect your pride

52:58.300 --> 53:00.302
and not wanting
to be embarrassed over all this.

53:01.678 --> 53:03.430
But I just want you to know…

53:05.807 --> 53:08.476
you don't have to try too hard
to act like you're okay.

53:13.148 --> 53:14.191
Okay?

53:19.779 --> 53:23.867
Oh, it's always so embarrassing
to be called out on your bluff, huh?

53:25.243 --> 53:27.871
Yeah, well… that's true.

53:28.455 --> 53:32.250
However, believe it or not,
I'm really relieved now.

53:34.753 --> 53:36.630
I feel like at least with this woman,

53:36.713 --> 53:40.675
I won't have to pretend
like everything's okay when it's not.

53:41.885 --> 53:45.847
I don't think it'll hurt,
even when I get closer to her.

53:48.391 --> 53:49.267
Right.

53:49.351 --> 53:51.895
Her. That's when you know
the right distance.

53:54.397 --> 53:57.359
"The right distance."

54:00.987 --> 54:02.822
Oh, I'm full.

54:04.866 --> 54:06.785
Let's wrap it up now, eh? Enough chitchat.

54:08.495 --> 54:09.329
Sorry?

54:10.330 --> 54:12.624
Let's rest. We have work tomorrow.

54:14.417 --> 54:16.169
Wait, you're saying I can sleep here?

54:16.253 --> 54:18.088
Who am I to say yes or no to that?

54:18.672 --> 54:20.715
Oh, and I snore at night.

54:21.299 --> 54:23.468
Oh, come on. That stuff's no problem.

55:19.691 --> 55:23.069
I already submitted the response
about the Ms. Kim situation.

55:23.153 --> 55:24.779
Oh, uh…

55:25.864 --> 55:26.990
Here, have this.

55:28.450 --> 55:30.535
- What's going on?
- Here.

55:33.496 --> 55:37.792
Uh, well, actually, you know
the chief editor of Munmin Daily?

55:38.501 --> 55:41.254
He read my column and, uh, he liked it.

55:41.338 --> 55:44.090
Now he wants me to write a feature article
for the newspaper next week.

55:44.174 --> 55:46.092
A feature article on weather.

55:47.010 --> 55:47.927
Okay, so?

55:48.720 --> 55:51.931
I was wondering if you were free to…

55:52.557 --> 55:54.601
I told you with the last one
that we were through.

55:54.684 --> 55:56.644
Just… just this once, Ha-kyung.

55:56.728 --> 55:58.355
I already told them that I'd do it.

55:58.938 --> 56:00.190
Okay, and so?

56:00.273 --> 56:02.984
All you have to do is just read it over
before I submit it.

56:03.068 --> 56:04.361
This is really the last time.

56:04.444 --> 56:06.196
Just one more time. Please, Ha-kyung.

56:06.279 --> 56:09.949
Hey. Does your wife know that you're
asking for all this stuff right now?

56:10.033 --> 56:12.452
What, uh… How could I tell her?

56:12.535 --> 56:14.120
You can't because
you're humiliated, right?

56:14.204 --> 56:15.622
Have a shred of that with me.

56:16.456 --> 56:17.457
Jin Ha-kyung.

56:18.500 --> 56:19.709
Hey, we're friends.

56:20.502 --> 56:21.461
Seriously?

56:21.544 --> 56:23.671
You and I have known each other
for ten years.

56:23.755 --> 56:25.882
We failed as lovers,
but doesn't our friendship remain?

56:25.965 --> 56:27.634
We spent so much time together
since college.

56:27.717 --> 56:30.970
The love is gone, but all
the other good memories are still there.

56:31.054 --> 56:33.223
- Don't you see that?
- No, I do not.

56:33.306 --> 56:35.809
I already forgot all my time
with you, Han Ki-jun.

56:35.892 --> 56:36.935
I feel nothing for you.

56:37.018 --> 56:38.353
Ha-kyung, hey.

56:39.062 --> 56:42.357
If you ask me about this anymore,
your wife's gonna hear about it.

56:45.527 --> 56:47.987
Jin Ha-kyung, how could you do this, huh?

56:48.571 --> 56:49.489
Ha-kyung!

56:50.323 --> 56:51.616
Director!

56:52.784 --> 56:55.203
What will I do?

56:55.829 --> 56:57.580
Oh…

57:05.046 --> 57:07.048
Good morning. The night watch is over.

57:07.632 --> 57:09.551
You're always a sunny spirit,
aren't you, Director?

57:10.135 --> 57:11.469
Oh, well, thanks.

57:11.553 --> 57:13.847
But I think there's something
that you should know about your team.

57:13.930 --> 57:16.266
Yes, there is a situation
going on with your teammates.

57:16.349 --> 57:17.559
My teammates?

57:18.226 --> 57:20.687
Haven't you heard,
they're living in the night-duty room?

57:20.770 --> 57:22.647
Oh, Mr. Um, yes.

57:22.730 --> 57:25.358
Forgive his situation.
He won't be there for too long.

57:26.067 --> 57:27.902
Everyone has a situation
around this place.

57:27.986 --> 57:29.988
One person alone hogging the bed is bad.

57:30.071 --> 57:32.782
But with two, where can
the night-duty team go?

57:35.034 --> 57:37.328
Did you just say "two"?

57:42.000 --> 57:44.127
Managing your teammates
is part of your job.

57:44.627 --> 57:46.880
Do you think Director Choi
would have let this happen?

57:49.591 --> 57:51.342
Lee Si-woo--

57:55.805 --> 57:57.640
- Oh…
- Um…

58:03.313 --> 58:04.939
Why are you two doing this?

58:05.523 --> 58:09.319
If you really don't have anywhere to stay,
go to a motel or a jjimjilbang.

58:09.402 --> 58:11.905
Well, you see, I have to come
to work early anyway,

58:11.988 --> 58:13.364
so I just need a place to sleep.

58:15.200 --> 58:16.701
It's weird to go
to a jjimjilbang in summer.

58:21.164 --> 58:22.707
Why are you not at the training center?

58:22.790 --> 58:25.460
Wasn't that where you were staying
during your apartment hunt?

58:26.085 --> 58:27.253
Well, that's--

58:27.337 --> 58:28.963
He got kicked out of there

58:29.047 --> 58:30.256
a few days ago.

58:31.966 --> 58:33.384
"A few days ago"?

58:33.968 --> 58:36.721
You're saying you've been staying
for a few days in the night-duty room?

58:36.804 --> 58:39.557
- Uh…
- No. He's only been here for two days.

58:39.641 --> 58:40.892
Before that, he was in his car.

58:42.393 --> 58:44.312
Hey, what the heck's wrong
with you, huh, man?

58:44.395 --> 58:45.563
Why would you tell…

58:47.774 --> 58:48.900
Wow.

58:50.235 --> 58:52.987
You know what, we're really okay.

58:53.488 --> 58:55.990
We'll take care of it,
and you don't have to worry at all.

58:56.074 --> 58:58.535
How could I not worry? How though?

58:58.618 --> 59:01.412
Everyone's coming to me 'cause they're mad
that you two are living down there.

59:01.996 --> 59:03.748
Why not say it directly to our faces?

59:03.831 --> 59:04.874
What are they saying?

59:04.958 --> 59:06.793
That I'm delinquent as a leader.

59:06.876 --> 59:09.337
They're asking how long
I'll neglect you two.

59:10.797 --> 59:11.798
Ah.

59:22.809 --> 59:24.936
What to do?

59:25.019 --> 59:28.106
Hey, Han Ki-jun.

59:28.773 --> 59:31.025
I heard you're writing
that feature for Munmin Daily.

59:32.235 --> 59:34.362
Uh, um…

59:34.445 --> 59:36.155
Yes. Yeah.

59:37.031 --> 59:40.410
I knew it. Your wife's power over you
is greater than mine.

59:41.244 --> 59:44.414
You were talking up and down about
how you'd never do it yesterday, huh?

59:44.497 --> 59:46.916
Of course, when your wife asks,
"Of course, ma'am, I will."

59:47.000 --> 59:49.836
I wouldn't say it quite like that.

59:50.545 --> 59:53.172
Wow, a sacrifice for love. Godspeed.

59:54.340 --> 59:55.800
- And good luck.
- Thanks.

59:57.677 --> 59:58.595
That's really nice.

01:00:00.305 --> 01:00:02.473
- Good luck.
- Way to go!

01:00:02.557 --> 01:00:06.102
Okay. Let's go!

01:00:11.608 --> 01:00:13.067
What do I do?

01:00:29.208 --> 01:00:30.752
Do I really have to do this?

01:00:33.630 --> 01:00:35.757
Yes, I do.

01:00:36.341 --> 01:00:38.134
Hmm. Let's do it.

01:00:39.594 --> 01:00:43.514
Reporter Chae Yu-jin's writing
got better after she got married.

01:00:44.766 --> 01:00:46.934
The title is really on point, too.

01:00:47.435 --> 01:00:49.854
Her husband works
at the KMA, you know.

01:00:50.688 --> 01:00:56.027
I heard a rumor that she was living
with a KMA employee before.

01:00:56.110 --> 01:00:59.280
I guess she ended up marrying that guy.

01:01:00.490 --> 01:01:02.659
Uh-huh. I heard that too.

01:01:03.534 --> 01:01:06.954
- Mm-hmm.
- I heard her husband's a good writer, huh?

01:01:08.956 --> 01:01:11.501
- Ooh!
- She really does have it all, doesn't she?

01:01:11.584 --> 01:01:13.920
Getting married
after living together?

01:01:14.629 --> 01:01:16.047
That's the right move.

01:01:16.130 --> 01:01:19.217
Oh, by the way, do you know
which division her husband's in?

01:01:21.219 --> 01:01:26.474
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:01:29.227 --> 01:01:33.398
I don't know about Forecaster Lee
but Mr. Um can go back to his family.

01:01:33.481 --> 01:01:34.399
Yeah.

01:01:34.941 --> 01:01:36.401
I wish I could just take him home.

01:01:36.484 --> 01:01:38.277
That, uh, would be hard with two kids.

01:01:38.903 --> 01:01:39.821
With three.

01:01:39.904 --> 01:01:41.739
'Cause my husband's beginning
a year of absence.

01:01:41.823 --> 01:01:42.782
Ah.

01:01:42.865 --> 01:01:44.033
Why not at your place?

01:01:44.617 --> 01:01:46.077
I think I'll be going now. Bye.

01:01:49.205 --> 01:01:50.957
It's not going to happen.

01:01:51.040 --> 01:01:53.543
The Assistant Director is so fastidious,
he never would.

01:01:53.626 --> 01:01:57.547
Well, I'm sorry for Director Jin
having this situation.

01:01:57.630 --> 01:01:59.716
I know.

01:02:05.138 --> 01:02:07.140
Ah, darn. This is still wet.

01:02:09.559 --> 01:02:10.977
What's car sleeping like?

01:02:11.060 --> 01:02:16.566
Well, except for the mosquito bites
and the neck cramps, it's not that rough.

01:02:17.233 --> 01:02:20.027
Ah, damn it. I hate mosquitoes.

01:02:43.926 --> 01:02:47.263
How am I supposed to sleep in here? Oh.

01:03:25.468 --> 01:03:26.886
Come in. What are you doing?

01:03:27.470 --> 01:03:28.805
- Oh…
- Okay.

01:03:31.432 --> 01:03:34.310
Mr. Um can take the study
along with your suitcase.

01:03:34.393 --> 01:03:35.645
And Mr. Lee will go there.

01:03:38.022 --> 01:03:40.024
It's really okay for us to stay?

01:03:40.107 --> 01:03:41.400
You're not here free of charge.

01:03:41.484 --> 01:03:44.654
I'm going to ask each of you
for a third of the utility fee.

01:03:44.737 --> 01:03:46.489
Hmm, one-third, huh?

01:03:47.240 --> 01:03:50.034
If you two don't like that,
then Mr. Um can go back home,

01:03:50.117 --> 01:03:51.786
and Mr. Lee can find a place of his own.

01:03:51.869 --> 01:03:54.080
Shouldn't we just stay at a motel, huh?

01:03:55.498 --> 01:03:57.375
Or maybe a jjimjilbang?

01:03:57.458 --> 01:04:00.711
Oh, yeah. That's more comfortable
than here, right?

01:04:00.795 --> 01:04:02.213
Uh, we'll be on our way, then.

01:04:02.713 --> 01:04:05.174
Is there some kind of tension with me?

01:04:05.258 --> 01:04:06.634
Hey, don't joke about that.

01:04:06.717 --> 01:04:09.929
Hey, no, that's ridiculous.

01:04:10.012 --> 01:04:11.973
If it's not that, you should stay.

01:04:12.056 --> 01:04:14.934
The pretext can be
the top minds of our team

01:04:15.017 --> 01:04:17.728
have formed a summer camp
for monsoon season.

01:04:17.812 --> 01:04:19.939
"Top minds"? So, even me?

01:04:20.022 --> 01:04:22.733
I think, for this one,
that's a little generous.

01:04:22.817 --> 01:04:24.610
Hey, no. Come on, eh. Don't you remember?

01:04:24.694 --> 01:04:27.405
I predicted the hailstorm
over the city back in March.

01:04:27.488 --> 01:04:29.323
That was luck, okay?

01:04:29.407 --> 01:04:30.783
Sheer beginner's luck, that's all.

01:04:30.867 --> 01:04:32.785
Don't forget I predicted
the rainstorms too.

01:04:33.369 --> 01:04:35.246
I think you two
are gonna drive me to drink.

01:04:37.331 --> 01:04:39.542
Uh, so I should grab some cold beers?

01:04:39.625 --> 01:04:41.836
Snacks too, okay?
Some dried squid or something?

01:04:41.919 --> 01:04:43.170
- Uh, yeah. For sure.
- Right.

01:04:43.254 --> 01:04:45.214
- I'll be back soon, okay?
- Uh-huh.

01:04:47.049 --> 01:04:47.967
Uh…

01:04:48.843 --> 01:04:49.927
The bathroom, huh?

01:04:50.011 --> 01:04:52.179
Uh, right over there.

01:04:52.263 --> 01:04:54.891
I'll use the master bathroom,
so that one's yours.

01:04:54.974 --> 01:04:56.767
Oh, thanks.

01:04:58.895 --> 01:05:00.021
Hey, uh…

01:05:00.771 --> 01:05:04.191
I'm sorry for the imposition, really.

01:05:04.275 --> 01:05:06.694
I'll find a place as soon as possible.

01:05:06.777 --> 01:05:07.695
Okay.

01:05:21.709 --> 01:05:23.544
Uh…

01:05:23.628 --> 01:05:26.589
What kind of beer would Mr. Um want?

01:06:09.674 --> 01:06:10.841
Oh!

01:06:19.350 --> 01:06:21.686
Oh, food girl! It's food girl.

01:06:33.447 --> 01:06:35.074
He should remember the code.

01:06:37.868 --> 01:06:38.995
That was quick.

01:06:40.913 --> 01:06:42.039
Ha-kyung.

01:06:43.374 --> 01:06:44.792
What are you doing here?

01:06:45.418 --> 01:06:47.336
I knew it. You were here.

01:06:47.920 --> 01:06:49.797
I had a feeling this was your home, huh?

01:06:49.880 --> 01:06:52.800
Who cares what you were thinking?
What do you want?

01:06:52.883 --> 01:06:54.260
It's just that…

01:06:55.720 --> 01:06:58.180
- I thought of you.
- What?

01:06:58.264 --> 01:07:00.433
Can I come in for a second?

01:07:00.516 --> 01:07:01.892
Are you crazy?

01:07:01.976 --> 01:07:04.937
How did you know how I feel?

01:07:05.021 --> 01:07:08.190
I feel like I am going crazy.

01:07:08.274 --> 01:07:11.527
I'm so tired.
Can I please just come inside?

01:07:11.610 --> 01:07:15.322
Ugh! Go home and tell your wife
about it, okay, man?

01:07:16.907 --> 01:07:20.578
I have something to say to you.
Just let me in. Let me in!

01:07:20.661 --> 01:07:22.413
You're not coming any closer!

01:07:22.496 --> 01:07:24.081
Is someone here?

01:07:25.666 --> 01:07:27.084
Who else is here?

01:07:28.169 --> 01:07:29.879
It's none of your concern. Just go back…

01:07:29.962 --> 01:07:32.173
- Uh-uh-uh…
- I hear a male voice.

01:07:32.256 --> 01:07:34.300
- Who is it, huh?
- Hey!

01:07:39.221 --> 01:07:43.100
I think I'm pretty drunk, man.

01:07:43.601 --> 01:07:45.102
Why are you here at this hour?

01:07:46.228 --> 01:07:49.648
Huh? Is that Mr. Um?
What is he doing here?

01:07:52.902 --> 01:07:54.445
Director Jin?

01:07:55.029 --> 01:07:56.405
Assistant Director Shin?

01:07:56.989 --> 01:07:58.407
Oh, Mr. Shin.

01:07:58.491 --> 01:08:00.493
How come you're here, Senior Forecaster?

01:08:01.118 --> 01:08:03.788
Well, because Director Jin told me
I could stay here with her.

01:08:03.871 --> 01:08:06.457
Oh, stay? You're with her.

01:08:07.041 --> 01:08:08.209
Oh…

01:08:08.292 --> 01:08:09.293
Uh…

01:08:09.960 --> 01:08:13.464
Uh, Director Jin, are you saying
this is your apartment?

01:08:14.548 --> 01:08:15.800
Yes, it is.

01:08:15.883 --> 01:08:17.551
Why are you here, Assistant Director?

01:08:17.635 --> 01:08:20.054
I live upstairs, 1302.

01:08:20.805 --> 01:08:21.722
Really?

01:08:22.348 --> 01:08:24.141
Uh, you two are neighbors, huh?

01:08:24.225 --> 01:08:27.186
Wait a minute. What's happening right now?

01:08:27.269 --> 01:08:29.355
Wait. Just wait a second.

01:08:29.855 --> 01:08:31.941
Doors opening.

01:08:36.278 --> 01:08:37.947
Oh, Seok-ho.

01:08:39.615 --> 01:08:41.492
Doors closing.

01:08:42.076 --> 01:08:42.910
You!

01:08:46.372 --> 01:08:47.957
Uh, what's going on here?

01:08:48.040 --> 01:08:49.542
That's what I want to know.

01:08:52.336 --> 01:08:54.755
Ha-kyung, what the hell's going on?

01:08:57.091 --> 01:09:00.678
The life is a sequence
of unexpected events.

01:09:05.724 --> 01:09:08.060
Why are all these people
in your apartment?

01:09:08.144 --> 01:09:09.812
Shut your mouth and just follow me.

01:09:11.605 --> 01:09:13.149
- How much more…
- Ha-kyung!

01:09:13.232 --> 01:09:17.486
…do we need to poke each other
before we figure out the optimal distance?

01:09:43.888 --> 01:09:46.557
You burst into my home in the middle
of the night to cause drama? Why?

01:09:46.640 --> 01:09:48.142
It's all my fault, Ha-kyung.

01:09:49.643 --> 01:09:51.103
My love Ha-kyung was…

01:09:51.187 --> 01:09:53.105
Wake up! This isn't okay!

01:09:53.189 --> 01:09:56.442
I'm so sorry, Ha-kyung.

01:09:57.610 --> 01:10:01.864
I like you more than anyone
I've known, and that's a little scary.

01:10:01.947 --> 01:10:04.241
How many reasons are there
for Han Ki-jun to see you?

01:10:04.325 --> 01:10:05.868
It seems endless.

01:10:07.077 --> 01:10:10.706
Well, can you guess
who in this building is her ex-boyfriend?

01:10:10.789 --> 01:10:13.959
This is all your fault!

01:10:15.669 --> 01:10:16.670
Damn!

01:10:16.754 --> 01:10:17.838
Lee Si-woo, quit it!
